# OpenSSL Configuration File — `.conf` Schema
#
# This file documents the OpenSSL configuration format used in
# `openssl-server.conf` for generating server certificates with
# Subject Alternative Names (SANs).

## File Extension
`.conf` — plain text, passed to `openssl req` via the `-config` flag.
OpenSSL's config format is INI-like with brackets for sections.

## Sections Used

```
[req]
distinguished_name = <section>    # Which section defines the DN fields
req_extensions = <section>        # Extensions to include in the CSR
x509_extensions = <section>       # Extensions to include in the self-signed cert
prompt = no                        # Don't prompt for DN values — read from file

[req_distinguished_name]
CN = <common-name>                 # Common Name for the certificate

[req_ext]                          # Extension definitions
subjectAltName = @<san-section>    # Reference to SAN list section

[san]
DNS.1 = <hostname>                 # DNS subject alternative name
IP.1 = <ip-address>                # IP subject alternative name
IP.2 = <ip-address>                # Additional IPs
```

## Behaviour

- `prompt = no` makes OpenSSL read DN values directly from the config instead
  of prompting interactively. If omitted, OpenSSL waits for stdin input.
- `req_extensions` applies to Certificate Signing Requests.
- `x509_extensions` applies when generating a self-signed certificate with
  `openssl req -x509`.
- The `@san` syntax references a section by name, not as a string.

## Key Points for Implementers

- The `DOCKER_HOST_IP` placeholder in the template MUST be replaced with
  the actual host IP before use. Both `IP.1 = 127.0.0.1` and the real IP
  are needed so Docker accepts connections from both localhost and external
  clients.
- OpenSSL's `openssl x509 -req` requires `-extfile` to pass extensions when
  signing a CSR — just having them in the CSR config is not enough.
- The server certificate uses `extendedKeyUsage = serverAuth` (implicit in
  the `san` section); the client certificate uses
  `extendedKeyUsage = clientAuth`.

